        "evidence": "No inflation. Substantive items found while reading are in the notes below.",
        "notes": "Flagged for the coordinating session, three items, none edited (all math): (1) Step 1's stated reason is checkably wrong. \"The eigenvalues q and -q^{-1} of sigma_i are swapped by *: q -> q^{-1}.\" Under q -> q^{-1} the value q becomes q^{-1} and -q^{-1} becomes -q; neither is the other member of the pair {q, -q^{-1}}. The map that swaps them is q -> -q^{-1}, which is the OTHER Hecke involution - the one that does induce lambda -> lambda' on Wedderburn blocks. The bar involution as defined in the proposition (sigma_i -> sigma_i^{-1}, q -> q^{-1}) is the Kazhdan-Lusztig bar, which preserves each block. So the conclusion *(e_lambda) = e_{lambda'} does not follow from the reason given, and may need the other involution. Scope (a): this is a defect in the stated justification, not a proof that the conclusion is false. (2) Step 3 assumes \"algebraically closed R\" and the displayed Wedderburn decomposition needs a splitting field, but the proposition only hypothesises a field of characteristic 0. Hypothesis mismatch. (3) \"d_lambda is the dimension of the lambda-isotypic component\" - d_lambda is dim V_lambda (the SYT count); the isotypic component has dimension d_lambda^2, which is what M_{d_lambda}(R) has."
